Explain a stable CLI error code

Usage: onequery explain [OPTIONS] <CODE>

Arguments:
  <CODE>  Explain this stable CLI error code [possible values: forbidden, invalid_request, login_denied, login_rate_limited, login_session_expired, not_logged_in, org_not_found, transport_error, decode_error, query_workflow_corrupt, query_workflow_internal, source_api_workflow_corrupt, source_api_workflow_internal, query_execution_failed, query_execution_timed_out, query_execution_unavailable, query_preparation_failed, query_rejected, source_api_describe_failed, source_api_execution_failed, source_api_execution_timed_out, source_api_forbidden, source_api_preparation_failed, source_api_execution_state_invalid, source_api_source_unavailable, source_not_found, source_name_conflict, source_query_interface_missing]

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Global Options:
      --org <ORG_SLUG>           Override the active org for this invocation
      --profile <PROFILE>        Select a local auth/config profile for this invocation
  -c, --config <KEY=VALUE>       Apply a raw config override for this invocation using `key=value`
      --request-id <REQUEST_ID>  Attach a caller-supplied request ID to outbound API requests
      --timeout <SECONDS>        Override the request timeout in seconds for this invocation
      --json                     Emit machine-readable JSON output
      --text                     Emit human-readable text output
      --verbose                  Emit workflow progress and retry tracing to stderr
